The issue exists when this information is setted in the `camera_info.proto` message. In this message you can find `Intrinsic` which is already fixed in this PR https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sensors/pull/281

```proto
message Intrinsics
{
  /// \brief 3x3 row-major matrix
  repeated double k = 1;
};
```

and you can also find the `projection matrix`.

```proto
message Projection
{
  /// \brief 3x4 row-major matrix
  repeated double p = 1;
};
```
When the SDF `<projection>` tag is not defined the projection values are setted to the defaults values, which means this would only work if the image has the same size as the default values `320x240`, otherwise these value must be different because this values (`fx`, `fy`, `cx` and `cy` depends on the image size). User might want to use the Intrinsic matrix or the projection matrix without checking if these values are correct. That's why if the projectin values are not defined we are using the value available in the Ogre(2) projection matrix.

